+@node RH850 FXU Built-in Functions
+@subsection RH850 FXU Built-in Functions
+
+With @option{-mfxu}, GCC provides a built-in function for each RH850
+FXU instruction.  The header @file{v850_fxu.h} defines the vector types
+@code{__v850_v4sf} (four @code{float}), @code{__v850_v4si} (four
+@code{int}) and @code{__v850_v4su} (four @code{unsigned int}), and the
+compatible names @code{__ev128_f32__}, @code{__ev128_create_f32},
+@code{__ev128_set_f32}, @code{__ev128_get_f32} and @code{__ev128_addfs}.
+An @code{int} argument after the vector operands is an immediate operand
+of the instruction and must be a constant in its range.  The functions
+whose names end in @code{i} operate on integer vectors.
+
+@defbuiltin{__v850_v4sf __builtin_v850_addf_s4 (__v850_v4sf, __v850_v4sf)}
+Generates the @code{addf.s4} instruction.
+@enddefbuiltin
+
+@defbuiltin{__v850_v4sf __builtin_v850_subf_s4 (__v850_v4sf, __v850_v4sf)}
+Generates the @code{subf.s4} instruction.
+@enddefbuiltin
+
+@defbuiltin{__v850_v4sf __builtin_v850_mulf_s4 (__v850_v4sf, __v850_v4sf)}
+Generates the @code{mulf.s4} instruction.
+@enddefbuiltin
